ts but we trained our we helped  our competitors train on this platform  so some people would say  that's not good business to help your  competitors what's flawed in their  thinking um they don't understand  business when you say what's good  business the best players in business  play for the good of the game  right that's what the infinite game is  it's for the good of the game and it and  it and at the end of the day the good of  the game means it's good for all  business  i mean at the end of the day um it's the  right thing to do from from a moral and  ethical standpoint like would was it  illegal for you to hoard your patents no  of course not would people have faulted  you for it maybe maybe not you know um  but did it build trust with people yes  will it make you uh the go-to uh company  of choice even if you're slightly more  expensive later down the road highly  likely will people come to you advice  and turn down somebody else who was more  finite and selfishly driven did you  demonstrate that you actually care about  other people other than yourselves yes  yes yes yes yes yes yes and in the short  term yes it costs you something of  course it did right in the long term  it'll pay dividends  way more than whatever whatever was  spent in the short term so i think  anybody who thinks it's a fool's errand  to do that who thinks that that's not  business all they're doing is revealing  themselves as finite players and all  they're doing is revealing themselves a  short-term mindset
 

